@bank all
// 0.99.7 (SC1 for lead 49): the words for TB6's hosted traditions (claude/p997-traditions, TRAD997_ON), in the crew's
// voices. They replace TB6's stand-ins (same keys and placeholders; the game falls back to the stand-ins when a key
// isn't here). Open lab: Dr. Imra Sato (fast and clever, in bursts, drifts off mid-thought; terrible tea). Spice shelf
// supper: Chef Auda Brennan ("love", warm, in charge, asks if you've eaten). Teach me your thing: Zeke (knitting),
// Tove (shy, knows plants by the week they were sown), Rina (dry, deadpan, undefeated at Tiles), Ravi (gentle, draws
// the comics wall). Bunk inspection: whichever officer walks it (plain, brisk, fair). Bread day: Brennan.
// (t997.spice-shelf-supper.notice keeps TB6's words: its {till} isn't a token lines_check knows.)
// A card line is said in the host's card (90 characters at most); coaching lines and the crowd are speech bubbles.

// ---- Open lab, Sato's card (in order: four lines, the question, your three replies and her answers, the close)
== t997.open-lab.line.1
- You came. Good. Gloves are in the box by the door. Touch only what I hand you.
== t997.open-lab.line.2
- This is where Survey lives between scans. Cold light, long benches, a label on everything.
== t997.open-lab.line.3
- Most of the job is waiting. Hours under the scope, then one small true thing. Worth it.
== t997.open-lab.line.4
- That's comet ice. Older than the sun, probably. And that one hums. Nobody knows why. Yet.
== t997.open-lab.ask
- Go on. Ask me something. Everyone gets one question. Make it a good one.
== t997.open-lab.pick.1
- What's the best part of the job?
== t997.open-lab.answer.1
- The first look. Nobody in all of history has seen that rock up close. Then you have.
== t997.open-lab.pick.2
- Why does the rock hum?
== t997.open-lab.answer.2
- Mori says it's the ship. I say it's the rock. Loser does the labels for a month.
== t997.open-lab.pick.3
- Could I work in here one day?
== t997.open-lab.answer.3
- If you like waiting, and writing small numbers neatly. Help at the next one. I mean it.
== t997.open-lab.close
- Right. Look round the island. Gently. They've been waiting a very long time.

// ---- Open lab: Sato, now and then, at her island (bubbles)
== t997.open-lab.show
- Dust from the Pale Shoals. Every grain has a number. I named about four hundred.
- Ice has rings, like a tree. Count them and you know how far it came.
- Hold it to your ear. Hear that? Mori can't. I hear it every time.
- We write down what we see, not what we hope. That's science, really.
- This one came off the hull. Hitched a ride for a week before we noticed.
- Label first, then look. Without a label it's just a rock.
- The green one's from a moon with no name yet. Mori vetoes all of mine.
- Gloves on. Not because it's dangerous. Because your fingers are greasy.
- That jar is a whole afternoon of the Shoals. It looks like nothing. It isn't.
- Hold your breath and it sparkles under the lamp. Go on. See?
== t997.open-lab.wrap
- That's the lab for tonight. Gloves back in the box. Thank you for asking things.

// ---- Open lab: the crowd round the island (bubbles)
== t997.open-lab.crowd
- Sato let me label one. I spelt it wrong. It's still in there, wrong.
- I never know what to ask. I just like looking.
- Is that the humming one? I thought it'd be bigger.
- Mori says the stripes are years. That's a lot of years.
- I touched the comet ice. Through glass. Still counts.
- Survey get the best rocks. Works get the best spanners. Fair.
- I learn one new word every time. Tonight's is "regolith".
- Don't breathe on the dust. I did once. Sato looked at me for a week.
- I'd work in here if it wasn't so quiet. I'd talk to the rocks.

// ---- Spice shelf supper, Brennan's card
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.line.1
- There you are, love. Dinner's done, so this is the fun bit. Sit, sit.
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.line.2
- That shelf's the crew's. Everyone brings a jar from home, name on the bottom.
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.line.3
- Once a week I take three down, eyes shut. A pinch of each. You taste, you guess whose.
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.ask
- Ever had a spice that tasted like home?
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.pick.1
- My gran's kitchen. Always.
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.answer.1
- Then bring a jar back from your next leave, love. It goes next to Kovac's paprika.
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.pick.2
- I'm not sure I'd know.
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.answer.2
- You will after tonight. Taste slowly. Your tongue knows more than you do.
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.pick.3
- Can I see the shelf?
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.answer.3
- After. Hands off the jars, mind. I know where every one of them lives.
== t997.spice-shelf-supper.dish
- three little tasting plates

// ---- Teach me your thing: each teacher's four coaching lines (bubbles, in order), the result's title and words
== teach997.torres-zeke.coach
- Needle in. Wool round. Pull it through. That's one.
- Not so tight. It's wool, not a mooring line.
- Look at that. A whole row. Wonky, but whole.
- Count them. Twelve? Twelve. Well done, you.
== teach997.torres-zeke.title
- Your first row
== teach997.torres-zeke.result
- You knitted your first row with Zeke. Wonky, he says, like his. Hobby: knitting, any seat.

== teach997.cruz-tove.coach
- Just under the joint. There. A clean cut. Good hands.
- Bottom leaves off. Gently. It needs its strength.
- Into the water. Mm. Now say hello to it. I mean it.
- That's yours now. Week-six mint. Don't drown it.
== teach997.cruz-tove.title
- Your mint cutting
== teach997.cruz-tove.result
- You took your first cutting with Tove: mint, in water. Tap a garden bed to grow more.

== teach997.rina.coach
- Your tiles at the bottom. Mine at the top. Don't touch mine.
- Three of a mark, side by side. That's a dock. That's points.
- Jump my tile and it's yours. Go on. Ha. Too slow.
- Seven. I win. You made me work for it, though.
== teach997.rina.title
- Your first game of Tiles
== teach997.rina.result
- You played your first game of Tiles with Rina. She won. She'd like you to know she won.

== teach997.hart-ravi.coach
- Box one. Someone wants something. Draw them.
- Box two. It goes wrong. Bigger. More wrong.
- Box three. Worse. Yes. That's properly worse.
- Box four. The duck. There it is. Perfect.
== teach997.hart-ravi.title
- Your first comic
== teach997.hart-ravi.result
- You drew your first four-box comic with Ravi. The duck's in box four. Hobby: drawing.

// ---- Bunk inspection: what the officer says at each check (by week), the result card, the verdict, the Mail's first words
== inspect997.uniform.ok
- Uniform: clean. Good.
- Uniform: pressed, even. Noted.
== inspect997.uniform.no
- Uniform: that's yesterday's, cadet.
- Uniform: I can see last night's dinner on it.
== inspect997.bed.ok
- Bed: made. Corners and all.
- Bed: tight enough to bounce a coin. Good.
== inspect997.bed.no
- Bed: not made.
- Bed: that's a nest, not a bunk.
== inspect997.locker.ok
- Locker: tidy.
- Locker: everything in, nothing on top. Good.
== inspect997.locker.no
- Locker: things on it, not in it.
- Locker: if it's on top, it isn't stowed.
== inspect997.title
- Bunk inspection
== inspect997.note.nod
- Passed: uniform, bed and locker all in order. Works reputation up.
== inspect997.note.uniform
- Not passed this week: your uniform wasn't clean. Next inspection: Thursday.
== inspect997.note.bed
- Not passed this week: your bed wasn't made. Next inspection: Thursday.
== inspect997.note.locker
- Not passed this week: your locker wasn't tidy. Next inspection: Thursday.
== inspect997.note.two
- Not passed this week: two of the three weren't right. Next inspection: Thursday.
== inspect997.note.none
- Not passed this week: uniform, bed and locker. Next inspection: Thursday.
== inspect997.verdict.nod
- That's a pass. Well done. Carry on.
== inspect997.verdict.uniform
- Not a pass this week. A clean uniform next Thursday, please.
== inspect997.verdict.bed
- Not a pass this week. Make the bed before you go, please.
== inspect997.verdict.locker
- Not a pass this week. In the locker, not on it.
== inspect997.verdict.two
- Not a pass this week. Two out of three. Let's get to three.
== inspect997.verdict.none
- Not a pass this week. Uniform, bed and locker. All three, next Thursday.
== inspect997.mail.pass
- Passed.
== inspect997.mail.fail
- Not passed this week.

// ---- Bread day: Brennan swaps your dough for a warm loaf
== t997.bread.title
- Your loaf
== t997.bread.give
- Here, love. First tins, still warm. Fair trade: yours feeds Monday.
== t997.bread.notice
- Brennan swaps your dough for a warm loaf. Tap any seat to sit down and eat it.
== t997.bread.later
- Your loaf's in Monday's basket, with your name on it. Your hands were full.
